  402:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "lcabadval (#518): the table-1 mutator, one named find/replace per mutant; MUTANT-TEXT-NOT-FOUND is a hard failure, so every edit doubles as a presence pin"),
  403:     "artifacts/lcabadval/killtable_20260910/mutate518b.py":
  404:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "lcabadval (#518): the table-1 mutator's second generation, for the mutants added after the round-one repair"),
  405:     "artifacts/lcabadval/killtable_20260910/summarize518.py":
  406:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "lcabadval (#518): the table-1 summariser -- reads scores out of the .raw logs rather than accepting any typed number"),
  407: 
  408:     # -- #520 alphatbinegsel -----------------------------------------------------------
  409:     #  The SHIPPED detector.  It is CLASS_DETECTOR and it is EXEMPT below rather than
  410:     #  wired, for a reason that is a fact about the battery and not a preference: NO GATE
  411:     #  IN THIS TREE RUNS AN ALPHA MACHINE.  `gate_crossfamily.sh' is the only gate that
  412:     #  mentions alpha at all and is therefore the named home; giving it one is a gate
  413:     #  change owing its own negative controls, which is a harness round, not a rider on a
  414:     #  CPU fix.  Filed to `wiringcliff', the row for exactly that question -- not left as
  415:     #  a silent third state.
  416:     # -- #521 mk48nvramkill ------------------------------------------------------------
  417:     #  CLASS_WITNESS, and correctly ungated: it is RED on the committed build by design
  418:     #  (15/47, all 32 kill rows failing), so a gate row would be permanently red until the
  419:     #  fix ships.  It is also NOT yet the round's detector -- its `msg census' row asserts
  420:     #  the DEFECT'S OWN SIGNATURE and is green only while the defect is present, so the
  421:     #  probe cannot score 47/47 on any build.  A shipped detector must drop or invert that
  422:     #  row first; until then this stays a witness of record.
  423:     "artifacts/mk48nvramkill/opus_mk48_nvram_witness_20260910.py":
  424:         (CLASS_WITNESS, "mk48nvramkill (#521): eight offsets inside the device's own 8192-byte registration reach a default: arm that calls exit(1) -- rung 3 on unmodified -E mvme88k -e mvme187, SIXTEEN cells driven (8 offsets x read/write), committed 15/47 with all 15 controls green, fixed 46/47"),
  425:     # -- #521 mk48nvramkill -------------------------------------------------------------
  426:     #  CLASS_DETECTOR, and EXEMPT below rather than wired.  It is a fast (0.4 s) single-leg
  427:     #  instrument that runs green on the fix today, so unlike a witness it COULD be gated --
  428:     #  what it lacks is a home: gate_m88k_rounding.sh is the only gate on this CPU family and
  429:     #  it drives luna88k, not mvme88k/mvme187.  Giving it an mvme187 leg is a gate change
  430:     #  owing its own negative controls, i.e. a harness round, not a rider on a device fix.
  431:     #  Filed to `wiringcliff'.
  432:     # -- ppcrldiclzero + siblings ------------------------------------------------------
  433:     #  CLASS_WITNESS and correctly ungated: RED on the committed build by design (19/27),
  434:     #  so a gate row would be permanently red until the fix ships.  It is also a FAMILY
  435:     #  instrument rather than a single-defect one -- it already reds on ppcrldimimask and
  436:     #  ppcrlwimiwidth, two further measured defects in the same handler family -- so its
  437:     #  contract needs stating carefully before any part of it is promoted to a detector.
  438:     "artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/opus_ppc_rldicl_witness_20260910.py":
  439:         (CLASS_WITNESS, "ppcrldiclzero: X(rldicl) writes ZERO on every execution -- rung 3 on unmodified -E bareppc / testppc / macppc -e g5, 190 of 190 census cells wrong on the committed build and 0 of 190 under the one-character repair (committed 19/27, fix 24/27).  Also carries a SECOND channel (the record form reports EQ always, so control flow is corrupted too) and rows for the two sibling defects it found"),
  440:     # -- #522 ppcrldiclzero -------------------------------------------------------------
  441:     #  CLASS_DETECTOR, EXEMPT below rather than wired.  It runs green on the fix in 0.2 s and
  442:     #  COULD be gated -- what it needs is a gate that instantiates a 64-bit PowerPC CPU, and
  443:     #  the two PowerPC gates both drive a 32-bit part, selected explicitly in their probes.
  444:     #  (A gate DOES construct 64-bit PowerPC CPUs -- gate 9 enumerates every machine subtype
  445:     #  -- but that is a CONSTRUCTION check with no result oracle.  Recorded because I had the
  446:     #  stronger, false version of this claim in three rows before a seat checked it.)
  447:     "ppc_rldicl_probe.py":
  448:         (CLASS_DETECTOR, "ppcrldiclzero (#522): 24 rows on unmodified -E bareppc.  A 190-cell (SH,MB) census, value rows at SH 0/8/32/63, a record-form CR0 row, a deliberately-vacuous cell showing where the vacuity boundary is, a negative-apparatus control asserting its own liveness oracle CAN go red, and a disassembler cross-check of every placed word.  BASE 24/24, null medium 16/24, EIGHT mutants 16-23/24, ZERO ESCAPES (killtable_20260910/t2/SCORES.txt)"),
  449: 
  450:     #  The frozen copies are the instruments as-run.  t1 is the 19-row form that pass 2
  451:     #  escaped TWICE; t2 is the 24-row closure; t0 is an apparatus failure kept on purpose.
  452:     "artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/killtable_20260910/t1/ppc_rldicl_probe.frozen.py":
  453:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "ppcrldiclzero (#522) table 1: the as-run 19-row instrument -- pass 2 escaped it TWICE at 19/19 (a shift-decode mutant it was blind to BY CONSTRUCTION, and a CR0 mutant that is the sibling handler's own shipping token)"),
  454:     "artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/killtable_20260910/t2/ppc_rldicl_probe.frozen.py":
  455:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "ppcrldiclzero (#522) table 2: the CLOSING 24-row instrument, byte-identical to the shipped regress/ppc_rldicl_probe.py"),
  456:     "artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/killtable_20260910/t0_apparatus_failure/ppc_rldicl_probe.frozen.py":
  457:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "ppcrldiclzero (#522) table 0: an APPARATUS FAILURE preserved rather than deleted -- the driver was derived by substitution from #521 and called THAT round's mutator, which replied `unknown mutant'.  The hard-fail refused rather than measuring an unmutated tree, but the table looked HALF-HEALTHY because both mutators define BASE and answered it identically.  No number from it is cited anywhere"),
  458: 
  459:     "artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/killtable_20260910/mutate.py":
  460:         (CLASS_TOOL, "ppcrldiclzero (#522): the mutator, nine mutants including the two that escaped pass 2.  Written with an editor rather than generated, because building it through a shell heredoc ate a backslash level and turned every escape into a real newline -- the carrier's documented trap, with its documented remedy"),
  461: 
  462:     #  The measuring seat's own apparatus, preserved with its answer.  Its mutator and mine
  463:     #  were written independently and produced the SAME figures, which is why the literals
  464:     #  were then reused verbatim -- so the legs stay comparable across the two tables.
  465:     "artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/pass2_20260910/opus_mutate.py":
  466:         (CLASS_TOOL, "ppcrldiclzero (#522) pass 2: the measuring seat's INDEPENDENT mutator -- six legs in its own clone, and the source of M_SH5 / M_MB5 / M_CR0"),
  467:     "artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/pass2_20260910/opus_probe_plus3.py":
  468:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "ppcrldiclzero (#522) pass 2: the candidate probe with the three repair rows, MEASURED by the seat at 24/24 base, 22/24 M_SH5, 23/24 M_CR0 before I applied them"),
  469:     #  Named `*_probe.py' but it is a PATCHER, not a probe -- it edits the probe rather than
  470:     #  asserting anything.  The checker's filename tooth is right to refuse `tool' here and I
  471:     #  am not renaming a seat's preserved artifact to satisfy it; RESEARCH is the honest class
  472:     #  for a script kept as evidence of how the candidate rows were produced.
  473:     "artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/pass2_20260910/opus_patch_probe.py":
  474:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "ppcrldiclzero (#522) pass 2: the seat's PATCHER for the candidate rows -- despite the name it asserts nothing; kept as evidence of how opus_probe_plus3.py was produced"),
  475:     "artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/pass2_20260910/t0_backslash_apparatus_failure/probe_plus3.BROKEN.py":
  476:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "ppcrldiclzero (#522) pass 2: THE SEAT'S OWN APPARATUS FAILURE, preserved rather than deleted -- a regex built through a non-raw string turned a backslash-b into a literal BACKSPACE, so the pattern matched nothing and failed a row on EVERY leg including BASE.  Two documented traps stacked into a confident wrong answer; the corrected run added a negative control so the regex cannot silently match nothing again"),
  477:     "mk48_nvram_probe.py":
  478:         (CLASS_DETECTOR, "mk48nvramkill (#521): 57 rows on unmodified -E mvme88k -e mvme187.  Sixteen kill cells (eight offsets x read/write), nine round-trip rows closing the survive-only class, a CSR rising-edge row for the control case's side effect, four device-signature controls in two encodings, and a negative-apparatus control that asserts its own liveness oracle CAN go red.  BASE 57/57, null medium 16/57, five mutants 16-56/57, ZERO ESCAPES (killtable_20260910/t3/SCORES.txt)"),
  479: 
  480:     #  The three FROZEN copies are the instruments as-run, one per table.  Evidence, not live
  481:     #  detectors: t1 is the 47-row form whose M_ICSR escape opened the floor breach, t2 the
  482:     #  48-row repair, t3 the 57-row closure.
  483:     "artifacts/mk48nvramkill/killtable_20260910/t1/mk48_nvram_probe.frozen.py":
  484:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "mk48nvramkill (#521) table 1: the as-run 47-row instrument -- M_ICSR escaped it 47/47, which is the floor breach the round was repaired for"),
  485:     "artifacts/mk48nvramkill/killtable_20260910/t2/mk48_nvram_probe.frozen.py":
  486:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "mk48nvramkill (#521) table 2: the as-run 48-row instrument after the csr-rise repair -- zero escapes, but pass 2 then found the SAME survive-only class on the eight accepted offsets"),
  487:     "artifacts/mk48nvramkill/killtable_20260910/t3/mk48_nvram_probe.frozen.py":
  488:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "mk48nvramkill (#521) table 3: the CLOSING 57-row instrument, byte-identical to the shipped regress/mk48_nvram_probe.py"),
  489: 
  490:     "artifacts/mk48nvramkill/killtable_20260910/mutate.py":
  491:         (CLASS_TOOL, "mk48nvramkill (#521): the mutator -- one named literal find/replace per mutant with MUTANT-TEXT-NOT-FOUND a hard failure.  ITS OWN PRESENCE PIN CAUGHT TWO MISTAKES: an ambiguous anchor matching twice, and an M_NULL that replaced a statement with a COMMENT so `goto ret' became the if-body and the leg measured a different mutant than the record claimed"),
  492:     "alpha_tbi_probe.py":
  493:         (CLASS_DETECTOR, "alphatbinegsel (#520): 15 rows closing the tbi selector guard's NINE axes -- the window's four sides, the interior, the negative selectors, a1 zero-vs-nonzero, a1 magnitude and a0 magnitude.  BASE 15/15, null medium 11/15, nine mutants 12-14/15 (killtable_20260910/t3/SCORES.txt); every accept row carries a measured kill, checked by tally_kills.py"),
  494: 
  495:     #  The three FROZEN copies are the instruments as-run, one per table.  They are
  496:     #  evidence, not live detectors: a citation into the live probe decays the moment the
  497:     #  probe grows, which is exactly what happened here -- it went from 7 rows to 15 and a
  498:     #  comment citing it for "5/7" came to CONTRADICT its own artifact.
  499:     "artifacts/alphatbinegsel/killtable_20260910/t1/alpha_tbi_probe.frozen.py":
  500:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "alphatbinegsel (#520) table 1: the as-run 10-row instrument -- M_D and M_E swept it, which is what the bound rows were added for"),
  501:     "artifacts/alphatbinegsel/killtable_20260910/t2/alpha_tbi_probe.frozen.py":
  502:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "alphatbinegsel (#520) table 2: the as-run 13-row instrument (probe_HEAD.raw 10/13, probe_BASE.raw 13/13) -- superseded when the pass-2 panel found the cast-width axis unrowed"),
  503:     "artifacts/alphatbinegsel/killtable_20260910/t3/alpha_tbi_probe.frozen.py":
  504:         (CLASS_RESEARCH, "alphatbinegsel (#520) table 3: the CLOSING 15-row instrument, byte-identical to the shipped regress/alpha_tbi_probe.py -- one instrument for all eleven legs"),
