  891: 
  892:     #  sgireunmapped #499: the SHIPPED detector.  Gate-run by gate_arm.sh -- invocation,
  893:     #  OPUS499T_DONE sentinel check, controls by name, EVERY row named individually, and
  894:     #  a SUMMED denominator that separates a LOST row from a FAILING one.
  895:     #
  896:     #  *** THE ROW COUNT IS NOT WRITTEN HERE.  It went 28 -> 34 -> 36 -> 48 across four
  897:     #  passes in one day and this comment said 28 for all of them.  Derive it: ***
  898:     #
  899:     #      awk '/for v in "live"/{l=$0; getline n;
  900:     #           if (n ~ /UNMLOG/) {print gsub(/"[^"]*"/,"",l)}}' regress/gate_arm.sh
  901:     #
  902:     #  The `getline'/UNMLOG pair is load-bearing and is not defensive clutter: several
  903:     #  sections of gate_arm.sh open with the same `for v in "live" "devsig"' names, so
  904:     #  the FIRST match is a different probe's list.  The log variable on the NEXT line
  905:     #  is the only thing that identifies which section a row list belongs to.  (A first
  906:     #  attempt here counted `check "sgi_re unmapped row:"' lines and returned 1 -- the
  907:     #  rows are named in a LOOP, so there is one such line however many rows exist.
  908:     #  It was caught by running it, which is the whole reason a deriver is written down
  909:     #  instead of a number.)
  910:     #
  911:     #  (Demoted literals, kept as the record of what was measured and never as current
  912:     #  claims: 18/28 pre-fix and 28/28 on the fix, the test-first evidence in this row's
  913:     #  own artifacts dir; 30/34 and 33/34 for the two pass-2 mutants against the 34-row
  914:     #  repair, where the 28-row version had scored both 28/28.)
  915:     #  #500 sgideprimop: the SHIPPED detector.  Gate-run by gate_arm.sh -- invocation,
  916:     #  OPUS500_DONE sentinel check, every row named individually, and a SUMMED denominator
  917:     #  that separates a LOST row from a FAILING one.
  918:     #
  919:     #  ROW COUNT NOT WRITTEN HERE.  The sibling entry below said "28 rows" through four
  920:     #  passes that took it to 50.  Derive it:
  921:     #
  922:     #      awk '/for v in "live"/{l=$0; getline n;
  923:     #           if (n ~ /PRIMLOG/) {print gsub(/"[^"]*"/,"",l)}}' regress/gate_arm.sh
  924:     #  pcc2widthkills: the WITNESS (rung 3, 4/10 on the committed build, preserved with its
  925:     #  run under artifacts/pcc2widthkills/) and the DETECTOR it grew into.  The witness is
