 1582: #  DATED, NAMED DEBT -- not a count and not a silent allowlist.  gate_offline.sh MEASURED that
 1583: #  a COUNT pin actively obstructs the shrink it claims to want ("6, shrinking not growing" went
 1584: #  RED at 5).  A date expires; shrinking is green by construction.
 1585: #
 1586: #  2026-09-20 matches the fbpending_bound:2026-09-20 deadline already standing in
 1587: #  gate_offline.sh's SM_EXEMPT, so #442's two debts fall due together.  IT IS A PROPOSAL: the
 1588: #  owner set the SM dates and set them TIGHTER than the ones proposed, and a deadline nobody
 1589: #  chose is a deadline nobody owns.
 1590: #
 1591: #  These are wiring jobs, not design ones -- each probe already prints a verdict token and
 1592: #  exits nonzero on failure.  What each needs is a gate that owns it, its rig preconditions,
 1593: #  and ONE clean gate run proving it green before it ships.  That last part is why they are
 1594: #  exempted here rather than wired here: gate_hygiene's own comments record FOUR probes that
 1595: #  shipped latently RED because the commit that added them never fired the gate.
 1596: EXEMPT = {
 1597:     #  pit8253_latch_probe.py's exemption is DISCHARGED, 2026-08-30 -- it is now wired into
 1598:     #  gate_arm.sh beside footbridge_sites_probe.py, which is the home gate_hygiene.sh's own
 1599:     #  bump note named for it ("wants an operator who can run that gate").  The entry is
 1600:     #  DELETED rather than dated forward, in the SAME edit that added the wiring, because a
 1601:     #  wired probe that keeps an exemption is a STALE EXEMPTION and this checker reds on it.
 1602:     #  Seven exemptions remain.
 1603:     #  sh4_bsc_width_probe.py's exemption is DISCHARGED, 2026-08-30 -- wired into
 1604:     #  gate_sh_rounding.sh, whose `-E landisk` machine it already used.  Deleted in the
 1605:     #  SAME edit as the wiring, because a wired probe that keeps an exemption is a
 1606:     #  STALE EXEMPTION.  Six exemptions remain.
 1607:     "fbpending_drain_probe.py": ("2026-09-20",
 1608:                                  "REPORT-ONLY by default: EXPECT_CAP must be set before a "
 1609:                                  "gate row can mean anything, so wiring is a design step first"),
 1610:     "hpcmips_ctor_probe.py":    ("2026-09-20",
 1611:                                  "rung 2, ~8 s, no rig image -- wants a construction gate"),
 1612:     #  Both #494 probes are TWO-LEG DIFFERENTIALS: they take a PRE-FIX binary and
 1613:     #  a post-fix one and compare.  No gate builds a second leg, so wiring them is
 1614:     #  a change to the instrument -- a single-leg mode asserting only the fix-side
 1615:     #  wants against the gate's own binary -- not a line in a gate script.
 1616:     "wdc_altoffset_probe.py":     ("2026-09-20",
 1617:                                    "two-leg differential; wants a single-leg mode "
 1618:                                    "before gate 10 can assert anything"),
 1619:     "wdc_altoffset_sig_probe.py": ("2026-09-20",
 1620:                                    "two-leg differential AND needs a ciR: CD-ROM rig "
 1621:                                    "the battery does not build today"),
 1622:     "wdc_altoffset_4bit_probe.py": ("2026-09-20",
 1623:                                     "two-leg differential; shares the single-leg-mode "
 1624:                                     "debt with its two siblings"),
 1625:     "wdc_addtoinbuf_probe.py":     ("2026-09-20",
 1626:                                     "two-leg differential AND needs a poisoned CD "
 1627:                                     "image the battery does not build"),
