79-are forward-only BY DATE because retro-failing an archive of hundreds of ledger rows gets the
80-rule switched off, and a disabled rule is worse than no rule.  That argument does not carry
81-here: the domain is a few dozen files in ONE FLAT DIRECTORY, enumerable in full today, and an
82-unwired probe has no date to be forward-only about.  A date cutoff would also grandfather the
83-four files this check exists for, permanently.  So nothing is grandfathered -- and the check is
84:still green on the day it lands, because each existing gap is written down as a DATED
85:EXEMPTION naming the round that owes it.  Debt that expires, not debt that disappears.
